es racing (a) a surviving reader, (b) another writer, (c) a held boundary. Keep the CR4 repairs green (surviving-reader convergence, first-open lock preservation, stale-generation refusal, revocation contention) and re-run the original seven reviewer probes. Note the reviewer bound on verifyLockFile's 500ms retry (custody rechecked, inode not pinned): document it as a stated bound or pin the inode, but do not claim protection against an owner replacing lock files externally unless you implement it.\\n\\nRetain rows 15 and 21 exactly as CR5 accounted them (Windows native tests present, runtime unverified; matcher-only, consumer handoff persisted); do not inflate them. Update the 21-row AC matrix with actual calls and named tests; rerun the hosttrust and config mutation batteries on the exact final source with per-plant raw logs, a neutral SURVIVED control applied through the same harness, exits from subprocess return codes, and no compile-failure/unapplied/empty-selection kills. Full configured local validation before the normal producer handoff; no hosted CI. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first. Leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED for the handoff snapshot. Attach TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev6.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md and TASK-260909-2ez769_producer-evidence-rev6.tar.gz, then hand off through task-board and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.\\n\\n===== TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-cr6.md =====\\nIndependently review Change Request revision 6 of TASK-260909-2ez769 (task_delta on managed checkpoint a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903, candidate tree b0bb3d9d600d4c323aa12480b3285512f96167c7, published by RUN-260916-44fc4f, 55 changed paths). This is the rework after the CR5 changes-requested verdict (TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev5.md, review-evidence-rev5.zip, review-logbook-rev5.md): read that verdict, the producer outcome TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev6.md, the census TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_producer-evidence-rev6.tar.gz, the rev6 patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. Superseded reviewer briefs (reviewer-cr5 and earlier) are historical; this brief governs.\\n\\nCR3, CR4 and CR5 were one family — a config/trust pair mutation outside the authorization transaction — so review the instrument first: the census must enumerate every production path that creates, replaces, removes or renames config.toml, its backups, trust.json, the pending joint-commit marker, the lock file and the credential files (the producer claims 12 rows) with lock state, intent revalidation, positive test, interleaving negative and narrowing plant; verify completeness against the source with your own walk (every caller of writeTempReplace, replaceDurably, secureStaged, CreateExclusive, os.Rename/Remove/Create in internal/config and internal/hosttrust), and verify that TestWritePathCensusGate actually sees a new unlocked caller (plant your own rogue caller in an isolated copy in a shape the producer's three control plants did not use — a new file, a method receiver, a var-bound helper — and confirm the gate fails). An undriven or uncensused row is a finding.\\n\\nThen verify the CR5 F1 repair: JointCommit now takes the restore closure and compensates under the same exclusive hold (compensateLocked: marker re-read and pin-compared, configuration hash equal to the replacement pin, restore, restored bytes re-read against the source pin, marker abort; committed trust deliberately not re-read), the unlocked restoreSourceAfterJointFailure is deleted, ErrJointReplacementDurable reports a clean abort and ErrJointCompensationFailed reports failed compensation with the marker kept. Rerun TestReviewerRestoreCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit on the exact candidate (the producer says its seam now blocks on flock; confirm that the final state can no longer be the CR5 failure and that the port TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit asserts the final state), and probe the six compensation race tests for apply and rollback against a surviving reader, another writer and a held boundary; decide whether \\\"never re-read committed trust\\\" can abort a bump that actually became durable and whether that is a safe refusal or a silent loss. Keep the seven original reviewer probes green.\\n\\nRetain rows 15 and 21 exactly as CR5 accounted them (Windows native tests present, runtime unverified; matcher-only, consumer handoff persisted); re-derive the 21-row AC table from source and named tests; check that the hosttrust (29+1 kills, neutral SURVIVED) and config batteries report exits from subprocess return codes with per-plant raw logs and no compile-failure/unapplied/empty-selection kills; confirm RPC backup 15/15 and parked 11/11 hashes and zero overlap with the candidate; confirm checkpointed SSH/peer predecessors are preserved and no RPC transport was implemented.\\n\\nMethod: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local. Attach TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev6.md and TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev6.zip, complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260909-2ez769, revision=6, evidence=TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev6.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2 classes and repeat-of named. Model: codex gpt-6-astra low. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.\\n\\n===== TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev6.md =====\\nRework the credentials/Config4 candidate of TASK-260909-2ez769 after the CR6 independent changes-requested verdict by RUN-260916-c3e675 (Astra low). Read TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev6.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_review-logbook-rev6.md and materialize TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev6.zip (probes TestReviewerLegacyCannotOverwriteCommittedV4, TestReviewerFailedReplacementCannotLoseIntent, TestReviewerFailedRollbackCannotLoseIntent, TestReviewerRoguePlantExecutes with the four plant files, logs). Base is still the managed checkpoint a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903; CR6 candidate tree b0bb3d9d600d4c323aa12480b3285512f96167c7 in .temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree — continue from it. Preserve the checkpointed SSH/peer leaves, the parked RPC artifacts and the control-root backup with their recorded hashes; no RPC transport; no manual commits; no direct .task-board edits; no self-acceptance. Superseded briefs are scope context only; this brief governs.\\n\\nThis is the fourth consecutive verdict in the config/trust transaction family (CR3, CR4, CR5, CR6), and CR6 shows the census instrument itself is not closing the class: the census exempted the legacy migrate writer (row 10) and the static gate detected 1 of 4 executable unlocked writers. Fix the instrument at the type level, not by adding names to a list: every helper that creates, replaces, removes or renames config.toml, its backups, trust.json, the pending joint-commit marker or the credential files must require an unexported exclusive-hold capability value that only the authorization lock acquisition path can construct (for example a *heldExclusive token returned by the lock and passed into writeTempReplace/replaceDurably/secureStaged/marker helpers and the raw os.Rename/Remove/Create call sites, all of which move behind that token), so an unlocked writer cannot compile; keep the static census gate as the second line and make it symbol-aware or fail-closed: unresolved writer references, package-level var-bound function literals, local aliases of the helpers, method receivers and os-qualified selectors reached through wrappers must all be violations unless the call site is one of the censused definitions, with the four reviewer plants (direct FuncDecl, package var function literal, local-variable alias, method receiver via wrapper calling os.Rename) plus your own fifth shape committed as executable controls that must fail the gate; document any writer that legitimately runs without the lock (credential fresh-key directories, lock creation) as a censused row with a proof that it cannot touch the committed pair.\\n\\nThen repair the two P1 rows against the census: F1 the legacy migrate path (internal/config/migration.go migrate) must run inside the authorization transaction with source revalidation under the lock (or refuse once any Config4 pair has been committed), so a delayed legacy Rename can never overwrite an admitted Config4 at an unchanged generation — port TestReviewerLegacyCannotOverwriteCommittedV4 RED first and keep it; F2 a failed replacement must never discard intent: JointCommit must not remove the pending marker on a replace error without proving from source/replacement pins which state is on disk; when the replacement rename succeeded and restoration failed, keep the marker (or converge forward) so readers refuse or converge instead of admitting a changed configuration at the old generation — port TestReviewerFailedReplacementCannotLoseIntent and TestReviewerFailedRollbackCannotLoseIntent RED first, cover apply and rollback, surviving readers and reopen, and keep the CR5 compensation races, the seven original probes and the CR4 repairs green.\\n\\nRetain rows 15 and 21 exactly as CR5/CR6 accounted them; update the 21-row AC matrix with actual calls and named tests; rerun the hosttrust and config mutation batteries on the exact final source with per-plant raw logs, a neutral SURVIVED control through the same harness, exits from subprocess return codes, and no compile-failure/unapplied/empty-selection kills; add narrowing plants for the token gate (a helper that accepts a nil token) and for both repaired rows. Full configured local validation before the normal producer handoff; no hosted CI. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first. Budget: the run has 4 hours and the runtime's own 26-command validation suite runs after your handoff, so hand off no later than 3 hours in; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED. Attach TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev7.md, TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev7.md and TASK-260909-2ez769_producer-evidence-rev7.tar.gz, then hand off through task-board and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.\\n\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 19390,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4848,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
